{#- Atlas — the way into the records (decisions 1, 2, 3, 15).

  Every Markdown record the build rendered, listed. Without this page the roadmap and the design
  authorities render at URLs nothing links to, and a site whose records cannot be reached fails
  Atlas's own premise invisibly — the pages exist, so nothing looks broken.

  It is generated from the same `site.documents` list the record pages themselves are rendered
  from, so it cannot list a page that was not written or omit one that was (decision 3: no
  artifact without a generator). Grouped by the directory each record lives in, because the
  repository's own shape is the only grouping Atlas is entitled to invent.

  Data this layout expects:
    groups — [{ dir, records: [{ title, path, url }] }], in path order
    project, repo, title — see base.njk
-#}
{% extends "base.njk" %}

{% block bodyClass %}page page-records{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
<p class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Project depth</a></p>
<h1>Records</h1>
<p class="lede">Every record in the repository, rendered as the file it already is. Atlas is never the record: where a page and its file disagree, the file is right.</p>

{% for group in groups %}
<section class="record-group">
<h2><code>{{ group.dir }}</code></h2>
<ul class="named-refs">
{% for entry in group.records %}
<li><a href="{{ entry.url }}">{{ entry.title }}</a> <span class="where">{{ entry.path }}</span></li>
{% endfor %}
</ul>
</section>
{% endfor %}
{% endblock %}
